verdicts.paired_ct:
Yes, same subject. Each patient has:
- a planning CT (Siemens Somatom Definition AS 64, per the README; 32 series including 2 replans), with RTSTRUCT, RTPLAN and RTDOSE;
- a reconstructed CBCT per imaged fraction (30 patient folders);
- one DICOM REG per fraction (160 files).

The README calls the REG files "Couch shifts used to align patients prior to treatment". They are clinical rigid setup registrations, not a curated deformable registration. The XIM headers also carry couch positions (CouchLat/Lng/Vrt/Rtn/Pit/Rol).
